source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons backup export -h <==
Write a backup to a .tar.zst file off this disk

Usage: omaddons backup export [OPTIONS] <ID> <FILE>

Arguments:
  <ID>    The backup: its id, or a prefix of 8 or more characters
  <FILE>  The file to write (a new one, in a folder that exists)

Examples:
  omaddons backup export 01M6Q2VA /run/media/me/usb/retail-wtf.tar.zst
    one backup, off this disk

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons backup export --help <==
Write a backup to a .tar.zst file off this disk

It never replaces a file.

Usage: omaddons backup export [OPTIONS] <ID> <FILE>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          The backup: its id, or a prefix of 8 or more characters

  <FILE>
          The file to write (a new one, in a folder that exists)

Examples:
  omaddons backup export 01M6Q2VA /run/media/me/usb/retail-wtf.tar.zst
  omaddons backup export 01M6Q2VA wtf.tar.zst --dry-run   what it would write

Writes one backup as a zstd-compressed tar: its description, its WTF/ with the modes
it recorded, and every file's SHA-256, checked against the backup's own hashes when it
has them. The same backup always exports to the same bytes. It never replaces a file,
writes nothing anywhere else, and refuses a destination inside a game client, a Wine
prefix or omaddons' own folders. It also reaches the backups of a client that is no
longer installed, so one can be kept before targets rm --purge deletes them. The
archive holds account and character names, as WTF/ does: keep it private.

See also: backup import, backup list

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
